{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1344568-post-your-durance-mk-2-electric-boogaloo","id":1344568,"title":"Post Your Durance Mk. 2: Electric Boogaloo","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-29T20:54:03-07:00","id":1344568,"title":"Post Your Durance Mk. 2: Electric Boogaloo","content":"Old version was fun and had great inspiration. but it's been dead for years now. So, I decided to make a new one. Enjoy<br /> <br /> Link to old thread:<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/990737-post-your-durance/page3\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-durance/page3</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T17:59:51-07:00","id":1344786,"title":"","content":"You never where interested in Romance, Aromatic Actually. But the Binder of souls didn\u2019t. Care. A certain True Fae Fancied themselves a \u201cMatchmaker\u201d taking people without romantic relationships and pairing them up, unfortunately being a Gentry they never Understood anything about Human relations,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T11:23:42-08:00","id":1346226,"title":"","content":"My second Changeling was a mechanic who accidentally agreed to make a car for a True Fae. He was tossed in a cage and was given basically only medieval era tech to work with. And while the TF always had the same aesthetic tastes, it would constantly change the law of physics in its domain at a whim. So one moment the spark plugs are working fine, next thing you know they're producing bubbles instead of electricity. Or now the wheels are trying to eat themselves, the gear shift moans when you touch it and the rear view mirror shows the past rather than whats behind you. This went on for YEARS. Adding to that TF would just show up for &quot;surprise inspections&quot; and would throw a temper tantrum when it confused your work in progress for the finished product and then proceed to destroy it in a fit of rage. Sending you all the way back to step one. Or turning your back for one second to see that the TF had replaced the pistons in your engines with miniature horses. Or suddenly being given surprise &quot;requests and edits&quot; that throw the entire project into disarray. Again this happened for YEARS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25700,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25700-gardenminttea","user":"gardenminttea","date":". 11-05-2019, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25700-gardenminttea","name":"gardenminttea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T12:32:56-08:00","id":1347536,"title":"","content":"His Keeper had named herself Greta Getemall. She took the form of a ten-year-old child, but beneath her spunky exterior buzzed a machine of relentless cruelty and ambition. Life with Greta was a neverending grind of gladiatorial battles as she traveled through the Hedge and the provinces of Arcadia, challenging other Gentry to test their captures against hers. Sometimes he lost, beaten into blessed unconsciousness until Greta deigned to revive him. Other times, he won, growing in strength and power in ways he never imagined. Between battles, he was kept in a tiny orb, hung from Greta's belt, dreading the next time she called out &quot;I choose you!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T03:18:28-08:00","id":1348199,"title":"","content":"One night, an actress who was part of a failing theatre group was alone upon the stage. She wasn't very good, but very driven to improve, and so was practicing by herself. Upon hearing a strange noise behind her, she turned to find a strange figure standing there. Her skin was painted in more colours than the world could hold, aside from her starkly white mask. The figure said she had been watching and looking for such a dilligent thing, and her voice was such sweet honey that the actress only noticed she'd stepped into the Painted Lady's world when she saw the thorns close behind her.<br /> <br /> The Painted Lady brought her to a grand theatre, and the actress found there was already another person there, another woman who had been brought by the Painted Lady in similar fashion. The Painted Lady asked them to perform upon the stage for her. Enchanted by her words they agreed, unable to fathom displeasing her. And yet, they did. The Painted Lady was not satisfied with her new actresses merely dressing up to perform their parts, or modulating their voices. That was not enough for her.<br /> <br /> She took the two to her workshop and stripped them, first of their clothes, then their skins. Strung up by their feet, they were left to bleed into a glass jar each--but it was not their blood, but their colour that bled from them. After a long time hurting, bleeding, hanging and eventually healing after a fashion, the Painted Lady returned to look upon them. Without their colour, their forms had become almost translucent, like the clearest water. The Painted Lady took the jars that held their colours and stored them away, then showed the pair a grand storage room filled with many jars, each filled with colours in kind. Using the colours of these jars, the two could change their forms to match whomever the colours had belonged to (for they suspected such must have been the case). However, they never saw their own colours again.<br /> <br /> Along with their colour, they had lost bits and pieces of themselves, now interchangeable with the roles they played. The Painted Lady was greatly pleased with the increase in their acting skills, which is not to say she did not often punish them to encourage them to do better. They would each play many roles, the colours bleeding off of them easily back into the jars when they wished it--however, each time they swapped their colours, a little of the pigment would stick to them still. Inevitably, it would accumulate to such a degree that they would have to be bled again, the Lady's other servants being left to separate out the colours so that each could be again restored to the proper jar.<br /> <br /> And so they spent day after day, thinking up and rehearsing new plays at a feverish pace to keep up with the Lady's demands. They had a feeling that if they failed to please her too often, their jars of colour would be all that would remain for the next two abductees to find.<br /> <br /> The Lady's foremost retainers were Light and Shade, who together brought the colours of her world to life. No other actors had ever survived the Lady's whims so long before, nor seemed so full of determination and life, and Light and Shade grew to love them. One night they found the pair in their cells, and gave them each a great gift: a mantle of deepest shadow for the actress, and a crown of brilliant light for her companion.<br /> <br /> Using the boons they had been granted, the two made their daring escape. But though the shadows hid them and the light dazzled the many guards set upon their path, they could not make it all the way out of the Lady's lands before being cornered by a force led by the Lady herself.<br /> <br /> Only one of them in the end made it back to Ironsides. With a skin clear as mirrors, she reflects the colours of others, still lacking her own. In Ironsides she plays many roles, and she learns them well. Though the scenes may change, it's always the same, grand play she is rehearsing. For her jar of colours is still within the Painted World, as is the lost companion who sacrificed herself to grant her a chance to escape, and one day, she will return for both.<br /> <br /> Perhaps then she will remember which of the two she is, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 11-13-2019, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}